  },
  {
    "unit_id": "u0029",
    "excerpt": "`SaveFormat` declares 21 values. **Seven are written.** The six PowerPoint\nformats \u2014 `PPTX`, `PPTM`, `PPSX`, `PPSM`, `POTX` and `POTM` \u2014 each produce a\ndistinct package declaring its own main-part content type, rather than one\npresentation package under six names; `MD` writes Markdown text.",
    "classification": "2_mechanism_explanation",
    "verification": {
      "status": "verified_against_source",
      "evidence_type": "clone_cache_path",
      "evidence_ref": "aspose/slides_foss/export/SaveFormat.py"
    },
    "disposition": "merged_reframed",
    "target_section": "Scope and Limitations"
  },
  {
    "unit_id": "u0030",
    "excerpt": "The other **fourteen raise `ValueError`**, naming the seven that work, rather\nthan writing a mislabelled file: `PPT`, `PPS`, `POT` (the binary PowerPoint\nfamily), `PDF`, `XPS`, `HTML`, `HTML5`, `SWF`, `TIFF`, `GIF` (rendering and\nconversion), `ODP`, `OTP`, `FODP` (OpenDocument) and `XML`.",
    "classification": "2_mechanism_explanation",
    "verification": {
      "status": "verified_against_source",
      "evidence_type": "clone_cache_path",
      "evidence_ref": "aspose/slides_foss/export/SaveFormat.py"
    },
    "disposition": "merged_reframed",
    "target_section": "Scope and Limitations"
  },
  {
    "unit_id": "u0031",
    "excerpt": "The following are not implemented, and the API member is absent rather than\npresent and inert:",
    "classification": "2_mechanism_explanation",
    "verification": {
      "status": "verified_against_source",
      "evidence_type": "clone_cache_path",
      "evidence_ref": "aspose/slides_foss/ShapeCollection.py"
    },
    "disposition": "merged_reframed",
    "target_section": "Scope and Limitations"
  },
  {
    "unit_id": "u0032",
    "excerpt": "- **Rendering and conversion of any kind** \u2014 no PDF, HTML, XPS or image export.\n  This is a design boundary, not a gap: the library writes OOXML, it does not\n  lay out or rasterize.",
    "classification": "2_mechanism_explanation",
    "verification": {
      "status": "verified_against_source",
      "evidence_type": "clone_cache_path",
      "evidence_ref": "aspose/slides_foss/export/SaveFormat.py"
    },
    "disposition": "merged_reframed",
    "target_section": "Scope and Limitations"
  },
  {
    "unit_id": "u0039",
    "excerpt": "`SaveFormat` and the file name are independent: `save(\"deck.pptx\",\nSaveFormat.POTX)` writes a genuine template under a `.pptx` name, and\nPowerPoint refuses to open a file whose extension disagrees with the format\ndeclared inside it. Give the file the extension of the format you asked for.",
    "classification": "2_mechanism_explanation",
    "verification": {
      "status": "verified_against_source",
      "evidence_type": "clone_cache_path",
      "evidence_ref": "aspose/slides_foss/Presentation.py"
    },
    "disposition": "merged_reframed",
    "target_section": "Scope and Limitations"
  },
  {
    "unit_id": "u0041",
    "excerpt": "Comment threads are written from the classic comment list on save. A deck\nauthored in PowerPoint can carry resolved status, @-mentions and reply chains\nthat the classic list cannot express; those are lost if the presentation's\ncomment authors are touched before saving. Loading and saving without going\nnear comments preserves the file's own threads untouched.",
    "classification": "2_mechanism_explanation",
    "verification": {
      "status": "verified_against_source",
      "evidence_type": "clone_cache_path",
      "evidence_ref": "aspose/slides_foss/Comment.py"
    },
    "disposition": "merged_reframed",
    "target_section": "Scope and Limitations"
  },
  {
    "unit_id": "u0042",
    "excerpt": "Unknown XML parts encountered during load are preserved verbatim on save \u2014\nopening and re-saving a file will never strip content this library does not yet understand.",
    "classification": "2_mechanism_explanation",
    "verification": {
      "status": "verified_against_source",
      "evidence_type": "clone_cache_path",
      "evidence_ref": "aspose/slides_foss/Presentation.py"
    },
    "disposition": "merged_reframed",
    "target_section": "Scope and Limitations"
  },
